# Pure SaaS Windsurf Rules
# Universal UI/UX Design System & Anti-Slop Discipline

When modifying or generating frontend components, styling, or layouts:
1. Universal Command: Use `/pure-saas [request]` or copy from `prompts/pure-saas.md` for any design, implementation, or refactoring task.
2. Specialized Subcommands (see prompts/ directory):
   - reference: Reverse-engineer visual reference via browser DevTools (prompts/reference.md)
   - design: Establish or update persistent DESIGN.md specification (prompts/design.md)
   - build: Execute complete working implementation (prompts/build.md)
   - audit: Quality audit across hierarchy, responsive, a11y, performance (prompts/audit.md)
   - fix: Remediate UI defects preserving backend APIs (prompts/fix.md)
   - polish: Raise visual craft, typography, and micro-interactions (prompts/polish.md)
   - responsive: Cross-device layout optimization (1440px, 768px, 375px) (prompts/responsive.md)
   - accessible: WCAG 2.2 AA accessibility and focus management (prompts/accessible.md)
   - motion: Purposeful transitions and reduced motion (prompts/motion.md)
   - tokens: Validate and export design tokens (prompts/tokens.md)
   - component: Reusable component engineering across 8 states (prompts/component.md)
   - verify: End-to-end verification and testing (prompts/verify.md)
   - system: Evolve product design foundations (prompts/system.md)
   - migrate: Modernize legacy styles without regressions (prompts/migrate.md)
3. Anti-Slop Discipline: Prohibit unapproved purple/cyan gradient text, excessive glassmorphism, monotonous 3-column cards, and emoji icons.
4. Semantic Tokens: Bind all styling to tokens in DESIGN.md. Validate with `node scripts/pure-saas.mjs validate DESIGN.md`.
5. Non-Regression: Preserve 100% of existing backend APIs, server actions, and database schemas.
